# Bash scripts must keep LF. A CR in the shebang line is a bad-interpreter error
# on Linux and macOS, and this repo is cloned with core.autocrlf=true on Windows,
# which would otherwise hand every checkout a CRLF script.
*.sh text eol=lf

# The Android shell is copied into the APK byte-for-byte, so a line-ending
# conversion in a checkout would change what ships. Git does convert tracked text
# here: src/META-INF/KRUSHI.SF and MANIFEST.MF came out of checkout 101 bytes
# larger than their blobs. These files have no NUL-free guarantee that git's
# binary sniff will catch every case, so they are declared binary explicitly.
src/AndroidManifest.xml binary
src/classes.dex binary
src/resources.arsc binary
src/META-INF/** binary
